<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">South African Defence Force</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1957–1994</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The South African Defence Force (SADF) was the armed forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a> from 1957 to 1994. It fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-african-border-war">South African Border War</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/namibia">Namibia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angola">Angola</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swapo">SWAPO</a>, the Angolan government and Cuban forces, and conducted raids into neighbouring states. In 1994 it was merged with the ANC and PAC <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> armies and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> forces to form the South African National Defence Force.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/south-african-defence-force.jpg" alt="South African Defence Force" width="320" height="215" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Air Force Ensign of South Africa (1981–1982).svg: *Ensign_of_the_South_African_Air_Force_1982-1994.svg: *Flag_of_Sout... · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ensign_of_the_South_African_Defence_Force_(1981%E2%80%931994).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
